A||||8||fierospeeder||watching an accident happen, almost.||||1||
Z||000000||fierospeeder||08-10-2000||08:08 PM||||I was going to college today, to pay half of my tuition bill.  I took my motorcycle, honda nighthawk 83 550.  While coming back home, i was going the speed limit, plus maybe 5 mph-10mph. So i dont get pulled over.  Not sure if my speedometer is bad but it seems a lot of people do pass me.<P>While going home, on a two lane street,<BR>I was on the left lane, while there was a pontiac boneville, not exactly sure, and a van behind that car on the right lane.  They both were going a little bit faster then me.  The bonnevile was past me about 2 car lenghts.  The Van ,contractor, was parallel to me.  While this is happening, the street goes into an incline and turns in a S form and theres a stoplight.  So the bonnevile was ahead of us, and i seen the light was red.  No it didn't change from yellow, it was just red.  <P>I was slowing down, and the van next to me also, it seemed as slow motion, and watching the bonnevile going through the red light at full speed.  While a lincoln towncar, having the right away, is going through the intersection at the same time.  The bonnevile almost slams right into the drivers side wheel, or driver, but luckily the towncar slams on his brakes and stops.  The bonnevile, seemed like it was going to hit for sure, and i would see a big wreck, swerves around the front end and drives off.<BR>The towncar driver, he had to be in his 50s or 60s looks paled as a ghost.  <P>I seen a crash like this on cops, while police were chasing a van, and the van hit a car on the side.<P>It just makes ya think, that you could be going the opposite direction, and some idiot doesn't pay attention.  Or if that was me on my bike and i would be sliding, no helmet yet, just a leather jacket.<P>anyone else seen close calls, or actual accidents.||||reg||1
Z||000001||FieroJon||08-10-2000||08:30 PM||||I had one similar to that just this week.  I was patiently waiting to make my left turn at a green light.  There was a truck in front and a car behind me.  Traffic was coming across the intersection both ways, and all of a sudden I look out my left window and see a Sebring convertable coming towards me.  Th guy (prob. in his 80's locks up the brakes, smoke rolling over the hood, and stopped about 3 feet from the truck's back bumper and my nose!  He looked around (like he wondered if anyone saw him) and backed up.  <P>------------------<BR>Silver '86 2M4||||reg||13
Z||000002||zeusrekning||08-10-2000||08:54 PM||||This may be my best post yet. I was staying with a friend at the local lake about 4 years ago. We went to his all star game and were going back to the lake that evening. We were laying down in the back of his dads truck half asleep. I feel the truck jerk and i pop up. As i look out the camper shell window i seen a small truck upside down in the air clip the top of a powerline pole. That was probably the most awesome thing i have ever seen not good awesome just shocking. <BR> off the side of the road was a hill about 4 feet tall going up about a 60 deg angle. the truck flew up the hill and started a barral roll. it landed on the wheels on the top of the hill.(it was flat) the guy was drunck. What had to hurt most was that the cab was full of fishing poles. Ouch||||reg||1
Z||000003||buds||08-10-2000||10:18 PM||||I have a totally graffic clip I can email people if you think you can handle it. The clip is of some guy getting nailllllled by a car while crossing the road. Buddy's a definite vegatable. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif"><P>------------------<BR>84 fiero se 2M8 5sp      74 corvette L82 4sp     98 Z-71 6.5 turbodiesel||||reg||1
Z||000004||wkayl||08-10-2000||10:52 PM||||About 6 years ago I was driving a Ford BroncoII.  I came over the top of a hill and a guy was passing a car uphill coming directly at me.  It was a 45 mph zone and the guy must have ben going 60.  I locked the brakes, cranked the wheel,rode the shoulder (3 ft dropoff) and hung on.  How he missed me I'll never know.<P>Another time with the same Bronco II, I was towing a '61 Studebaker Lark on a tow dolly in the winter in NE S. Dak.  I hit black ice under snow doing 60mph.  The Studebaker started to fishtail.  I could see the whole side of it in my sideview mirror.  I fought it untill I decided that it wasn't IF we were going into the ditch, but WHEN.  An approach was ahead so I figured if I could get past that maybe it would only wreck one of the vehicles.  As I was about to give up the fight, for some reason I punched the gas (it was locked in 4 wheel drive).  It pulled straight and true.  I pulled over and stopped and 2 minutes later a snowplow came from the other direction.  I had heard of people being so scared they couldn't stand, but I never believed it untill then.  I had to hang on to the car to keep from falling to my knees.  Why I thought of nailing the gas I'll never know.  It may be from watching monster trucks and them sayng that is what they do to pull out of a skid.||||reg||1
Z||000005||fiero56||08-11-2000||12:05 AM||||This just happened the other day. About 9AM(fairly heavy traffic) I am driving down the highway behind a newer blue chevy van. We both merge over into the exit ramp and I begin to slow down(short exit ramp to a busy intersection). The brake lights on the van come on, flash a couple times, and it swerves off the ramp into the grass and crashes into a grass embankment(side of overpass). I stopped to make sure the driver was ok, he was, but it turns out the brakes in the van all of a sudden quit. He was smart enough not to plow into the dozen cars ahead of him, so he swerved off the road, just missing the cars, and crashed it into a steep grassy hill. Luckily the guy was unhurt, but I was amazed at the dozens of cars driving by, and the people waiting at the stoplight 5 yards away, just staring at this guy who has just crashed a van into a hill at 60mph, and no-one did a thing about it. They just stared until the light turned green and they went on with their life. I couldn't believe it. I was just so mad at them.||||reg||1
Z||000006||AkursedX||08-11-2000||01:58 AM||||This was probably one of the scariest moments of my life.<BR>I was on my way to school one day.  It was an evening class so it was rush-hour traffic.<BR>Well there's a traffic signal on the expressway that gets real crowded at this time, so I was stuck real far back in line in the left lane.  Well I'm just sitting there and I look in my rear-view mirror, and I see this guy in a minivan flying at about 70mph towards me.  I'm thinking to myself "There is no way in hell he is gonna stop in time" So I pull over as far as I can to the concrete barrier and close my eyes.  Well I heard his tires start skreeching.  I open my eyes and I see him flying by me as he swerved into the other lane.  He had to miss me by inches.<P>There is one part I left out, as I was looking at him in my rear view mirror I this guy talking on his cell phone!!  Well I managed to pull up next to him as the light turned red again and he had his window rolled down, so I rolled down mine and explained to him about the dangers of cell phone use while operating your vechicle.  One of those dangers being me coming out of my car and beating the living **** out of him.  Needless to say, I was just a bit irritated.||||reg||8
Z||000007||Taijiguy||08-11-2000||02:52 PM||||OK, here's a couple:<P>This is minor, and probably doesn't even count, but it was pretty funny. I was on my way home from my girlfriends' house. It was a residential street, no sidewalk, just a gravel berm on either side. These two wiseass kids are on bikes riding down like, the MIDDLE of my lane, one in front of the other, just being irritating, not getting over to let me pass. So I'm waiting very patiently for trafic to clear so I can get over and go around. The kid in front is looking back at me with this idignant look on his face, basically taunting me. Then his buddy gets the same idea, and looks back at me. About this time traffic clears, I start to slowly pull over, when the kid in front suddenly seems to remember he's moving, and should look where he's going, when he turns back forward, he wobbles the bike and hits his brakes, his buddy, still giving me the look, crashes right into the back of his buddy and they both go down! I laffed my hiney off. I thought, "now there's poetic justice..."<P>OK, so waaaaay back in like, '83, I had a BEAUTIFUL Kelmark (kit car, Dino replica) and was driving across I-85 in Pensylvania, on my way to visit the 'rents. Pretty much without warning, the right lane merges into the left lane due to some construction. Now, I've been rear ended more times than I can count, so I have this habit of looking in my rear view mirror whenever I have to stop, to see what's behind me. And that's exactly what I did when traffic started to merge. I could see that about a quarter mile behind me was the next car in line, not much traffic) and he was coming up fast. I could tell he wasn't about to stop. I watch in horror as he kept coming. Suddenly my survival instinct took over, I slammed the car in gear, pushed the accerator pedal as hard as I could, dumped the clutch, smoking the tires, cranked the wheel hard right, and drove right over the pylons blocking the right lane. Just about the time I cleared the lane the guy in the truck came through and shoved the three cars that had been in front of me into each other...bam bam bam. Had I been in the middle of that with that fiberglass bodied car, I would surely have been killed. I guess it was good I had been rear ended all those times before, since they are what cultivated that habit of checking my mirror at stops.<P>-Taiji||||reg||1
Z||000008||whamel||08-11-2000||04:52 PM||||Last weekend - I was towing my newly acquired Acura Integra back from Detroit on I-94 on a tow dolly.  I was following a huge Ford truck who had a very heavy trailer and there was another guy with a Toyota truck with a boat on a trailer.  I have to also mention that there was a Nissan Maxima directly in front of me between the huge Ford.  I have to admit, we were probably all going a bit over the speed limit and sticking a little too close together, but traffic was flowing nicely and sometimes it happens.  All of a sudden this moron in a smallish red car cuts down the right lane so he can cut off the Ford truck, then stop and crank it onto the shoulder so he can get into the emergency vehicles only lane to turn around.  I just have to say that all of the other drivers did an awesome job of handling this!!  It could have been quite the catastrophy all things considered.  All I could think of at the time was...drat these stupid Firestone Wilderness AT tires I have.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  I was sure they were going to explode!  I just hope I have an easier time towing that GT back from PA next weekend.||||reg||1
